This directory holds the bundled piicatcher sidecar binary.

Tauri expects the file `piicatcher-<target-triple>` (e.g.
`piicatcher-aarch64-apple-darwin` on Apple Silicon, `piicatcher-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.exe`
on Windows). It is produced by `desktop/scripts/build-piicatcher-sidecar.sh`
and gitignored — never commit a generated binary.

For local development you don't need this file: the Rust shell falls back to
`piicatcher` on PATH (or to `$PIICATCHER_BIN`). The sidecar is only required
for production `tauri build` invocations.
